<title>FRANCE: Dior to control Japan distribution.</title>
<headline>Dior to control Japan distribution.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christian Dior Couture, a subsidiary of Christian Dior, said on Friday that it would assume control of the distribution of its imports in Japan, previously handled by a franchise held by Kanebo.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the boutiques in Japan would be transferred in April from Kanebo to Christian Dior KK, a wholly owned Christian Dior unit created for this purpose.</p>
<p>Under the terms of a new accord between Dior and Kanebo, Kanebo will continue to produce children's and men's clothes under licence from Dior but will stop producing ready-to-wear for women and accessories as of the autumn of 1997.</p>
</text>
